---
const checks = [
  ['Buying channel', 'GEP SMART materials describe catalog, inventory and PunchOut search. Confirm the buyer intends to expose this supplier through a PunchOut source rather than a hosted catalog.'],
  ['PunchOut protocol', 'GEP’s PunchOut guide discusses cXML and OCI generally. Obtain this buyer’s selected protocol, credentials and cart-return specification.'],
  ['Supplier storefront', 'Map the buyer connection to the Shopify store and catalog access that should be available in the PunchOut session.'],
  ['PO and invoice route', 'Confirm how an approved GEP purchase order reaches PunchOut Central, and whether invoicing uses a separate buyer process.']
];
---
<main>
  <section class="page-hero page-hero--mint" id="overview"><div class="wrap page-hero__grid">
    <div class="page-hero__copy reveal"><span class="ey">Shopify GEP SMART PunchOut</span><h1>Connect a GEP SMART PunchOut buyer to Shopify.</h1><p class="lead">GEP SMART includes supplier PunchOut sites among its catalog options. PunchOut Central connects a configured buyer session to your Shopify storefront; the buyer’s exact protocol and order-delivery path must be established during onboarding.</p><div class="page-hero__actions"><a class="btn pri" href="/book-demo/">Discuss a GEP buyer &rarr;</a><a class="btn secbtn" href="#details">Review setup &darr;</a></div></div>
    <div class="hero-visual logo-hero reveal"><div class="hero-visual__label"><span>Buyer system</span><b>PunchOut source</b></div><div class="logo-hero__mark"><strong>GEP SMART</strong></div><span class="logo-hero__status">PunchOut Central</span><h3>GEP to Shopify</h3><p>Supplier catalog access through buyer procurement.</p></div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="sec" id="flow"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head center reveal"><span class="ey">GEP SMART buying</span><h2>Use the PunchOut path when the buyer needs a live catalog.</h2><p class="lead">GEP SMART describes hosted catalogs and supplier PunchOut sites as separate buying sources. In a PunchOut session, the supplier’s Shopify store supplies the catalog while the buyer retains requisition and approval control.</p></div>
    <div class="integration-flow reveal"><div class="integration-node"><strong>GEP SMART</strong><span>Buyer shopping and approval</span></div><div class="integration-arrow">&rarr;</div><div class="integration-node integration-node--accent"><strong>PunchOut Central</strong><span>Connection and transaction</span></div><div class="integration-arrow">&rarr;</div><div class="integration-node"><strong>Shopify</strong><span>Supplier catalog and order</span></div></div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="sec soft" id="details"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head reveal"><span class="ey">Supplier onboarding</span><h2>Specify the GEP catalog type and message flow.</h2><p class="lead">Do not infer the buyer’s protocol from the platform name. Confirm how this GEP environment starts PunchOut, returns cart items, issues the approved PO and accepts invoices.</p></div>
    <div class="simple-steps">{checks.map(([title, description], index) => <article class="simple-step reveal"><span class="simple-step__num">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{description}</p></article>)}</div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="sec" id="proof"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head reveal"><span class="ey">Buyer testing</span><h2>Prove the cart-to-PO boundary.</h2><p class="lead">Test the GEP PunchOut entry, Shopify catalog access, returned cart, requisition approval and approved PO. PunchOut Central should create the Shopify order only after PO receipt; invoice activity must be checked against the buyer’s selected channel.</p></div>
    <div class="related-grid"><a class="related-card reveal" href="/integrations/shopify/"><span>Supplier side</span><h3>Shopify integration</h3><p>See how the live catalog is used.</p><b>Explore &rarr;</b></a><a class="related-card reveal" href="/integrations/cxml/"><span>Protocol</span><h3>cXML PunchOut</h3><p>Explore one supported protocol.</p><b>Explore &rarr;</b></a><a class="related-card reveal" href="/integrations/oci/"><span>Protocol</span><h3>OCI PunchOut</h3><p>Explore the other supported protocol.</p><b>Explore &rarr;</b></a></div>
    <p><small>Buyer-side references: <a href="https://www.gep.com/brochure/download/160/1874">GEP SMART catalog management fact sheet</a> and <a href="https://www.gep.com/info-guide/punchout-catalogs-guide">GEP’s PunchOut catalog guide</a>.</small></p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="sec soft" id="faq"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head center reveal"><span class="ey">FAQ</span><h2>GEP SMART questions</h2></div><div class="faq reveal">
    <div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>Is this a hosted GEP catalog?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>No. This page addresses a PunchOut source that opens the supplier’s existing Shopify catalog. The buyer must select that buying channel.</p></div></div>
    <div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>Is cXML or OCI guaranteed for every GEP buyer?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>No. GEP discusses both protocols in its PunchOut guidance, but the protocol for a particular GEP SMART connection must be confirmed with the buyer.</p></div></div>
    <div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>Does cart return create the Shopify order?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>No. The returned cart remains in the buyer’s procurement flow. The approved PO is the handoff for store-order creation.</p></div></div>
  </div></div></section>
  <section class="page-cta"><div class="wrap reveal"><span class="ey">Map a GEP connection</span><h2>Review the buyer’s PunchOut and PO specifications.</h2><p class="lead">Share the GEP SMART configuration and your Shopify catalog details.</p><div class="page-hero__actions"><a class="btn pri" href="/book-demo/">Book a demo &rarr;</a><a class="btn secbtn" href="/integrations/procurement-systems/">Explore buyer systems</a></div></div></section>
</main>
